What if `offset == nbytes - 2`? Then `src = s + nbytes - 2 + 1 = s + nbytes - 1 = esrc - 1`. The loop condition `src < esrc` is true, so it enters the loop. `*src` reads `*(s + nbytes - 1)` which is the last byte. Then `*(src - 1)` reads `*(s + nbytes - 2)` which is valid. Then `src += 2` makes `src = esrc + 1`, and the loop exits. This is fine.

